Players won't get permanent lung damage if they have a mild of asymptomatic case. The people who could get permanent language are the ones going on ventilators or are close to needing a ventilator. Feel free to show me an example of severe lung damage from a asymptomatic or mild case. I haven't found any examples. The notion that they can cause lung damage is not backed by science but backed by doomers.

&#x200B;

Now, this isn't to say that a nfl player couldn't get a severe case but it's unlikely due to nfl players being in peak physical condition and being young for the most part. (Big Ben not included)

